{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Java and Python SDKs will be implemented as thin wrappers around existing Fabric gRPC client interfaces, with no modifications to core Fabric protocol or consensus logic.",
    "Pre-built user chaincode will be distributed as Docker images for common Fabric network environments (linux/amd64, linux/arm64 etc.), with peer configuration to specify a target container registry for image pulls, eliminating the need for on-peer chaincode building.",
    "VSCC validation failure details will be logged at INFO level (instead of only DEBUG) and exposed via existing Fabric event hub APIs by extending existing failure event payloads, with no new event infrastructure required.",
    "Fabric tool binaries will be built using native Go cross-compilation support, with releases published as GitHub release assets for Linux (amd64, arm64), macOS (amd64, arm64), and Windows (amd64) platforms.",
    "Certificate fingerprint validation will be implemented as an optional, opt-in per-organization feature configured via channel config, with two supported modes: endorsement-time fetching of org-hosted fingerprint lists, and channel-loaded signed fingerprint lists to avoid endorsement-time non-determinism.",
    "Test network quick start documentation will leverage existing functional Docker Compose scripts in the fabric/test/ directory, with only a simple entrypoint script and documentation updates required, no new test network tooling is developed.",
    "Default configuration values will be extracted directly from Fabric source code into YAML files in a new config_defaults/ directory, with one file per core component (peer, orderer, configtx, etc.), and the existing sampleconfig/ directory will be deprecated but retained for backward compatibility."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The 'so I develop application with NodeJS' text in user stories U1 and U2 is a copy-paste error; the actual requirements are for a Java SDK (U1) and Python SDK (U2) for Fabric application development, respectively.",
    "All development is based on the existing Hyperledger Fabric v2.x codebase, with no requirement for backward compatibility with Fabric v1.x versions.",
    "For pre-built chaincode deployment (U3), a configurable standard Docker registry (public or private) is available for storing chaincode images; no new registry service is developed as part of this increment.",
    "The existing Fabric event hub infrastructure is sufficient to expose VSCC validation failure details, with no need for new event types or messaging infrastructure.",
    "All Fabric tools are implemented in Go, so native cross-compilation is supported without additional build tooling or dependencies.",
    "For certificate fingerprint validation (U6), organizations opting into the feature are responsible for the availability and security of their fingerprint list endpoints (for endorsement-time mode) or the security of their fingerprint list signing keys (for channel-loaded mode); no additional high availability or key management features are included in this increment.",
    "Existing test network scripts in the fabric/test/ directory are fully functional; the test network quick start (U7) only requires documentation updates and a simple entrypoint script, no new test network tooling or script rewrites are needed.",
    "The existing fabric/sampleconfig/ directory will be deprecated but not removed in this increment to avoid breaking existing users who reference it."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Develop Java SDK for Hyperledger Fabric",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a Java SDK wrapping Fabric gRPC APIs to support channel management, transaction submission, event listening, and ledger queries for application developers. Includes unit and integration tests, and basic getting started documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Develop Python SDK for Hyperledger Fabric",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a Python SDK wrapping Fabric gRPC APIs with idiomatic Python interfaces for core Fabric functionality (channel management, transaction submission, event listening, ledger queries). Includes unit and integration tests, and basic getting started documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement pre-built user chaincode deployment support",
      "activity_description": "Modify peer chaincode deployment logic to support pulling pre-built Docker images of user chaincode (for common Fabric network environments) from a configurable container registry, eliminating the need for peers to build chaincode from source. Includes configuration options, integration tests, and documentation updates.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Enhance VSCC validation logging and failure event exposure",
      "activity_description": "Modify VSCC validation logic to log policy details, signer peer/org names, and missing signers at INFO level. Extend existing Fabric event payloads to include VSCC validation failure details for SDK and external process consumption. Includes unit and integration tests, and documentation updates.",
      "most_likely_effort": 72
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Build and publish platform-specific Fabric tool binaries",
      "activity_description": "Set up cross-compilation pipelines for Linux (amd64, arm64), macOS (amd64, arm64), and Windows (amd64) for all Fabric tools (configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca client, etc.). Test cross-compiled binaries, generate release assets with checksums, and update download documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 72
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement certificate fingerprint validation for channel members",
      "activity_description": "Add optional per-organization certificate fingerprint validation support, including endorsement-time fetching of org-controlled fingerprint lists and channel-loaded signed fingerprint list options. Integrate validation into the peer endorsement flow, add configuration options, and include integration tests and documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 128
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Create test network quick start documentation",
      "activity_description": "Develop a simple entrypoint script to spin up a local Fabric test network, document common test operations in the official Fabric testing docs, add links to relevant test/ subdirectory readmes, and update test/ subdirectory README files as needed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Consolidate default component configurations",
      "activity_description": "Extract all default configuration values from Fabric source code into YAML files in a new config_defaults/ directory (including core.yaml, orderer.yaml, configtx.yaml etc.), update all documentation and Build Your First Network (BYFN) scripts to reference these files, and validate completeness of captured default values.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 640
  }
}

